1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,500
This demo shows how an LLM and a VLM coordinate five UAVs for river inspection.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:12,500
The LLM plans tasks and routes; the VLM detects anomalies in on-site images and videos.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,100
Five UAVs take off to begin the river inspection.

4
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:29,000
The LLM divides the river into coverage areas and assigns one to each UAV.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Five onboard camera feeds show the scene in real time on the right.

6
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:21,000
The five UAVs head toward their assigned areas.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The LLM decides where each UAV should patrol; the VLM identifies where closer inspection is needed.

8
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:06,000
The five highlighted target routes show the initial patrol areas planned by the LLM.

9
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Each UAV follows its assigned inspection route.

10
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:49,500
VLM inference reveals a bridge obstacle; UAV 3 reroutes to circle the bridge.

11
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:05,000
UAV 3 leaves a coverage gap to inspect the bridge, so the LLM replans routes for UAVs 2 and 4.

12
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Following the LLM's new plan, UAVs 2 and 4 expand their patrol areas to cover the gap left by UAV 3.

13
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:31,000
UAV 3 inspects the bridge while UAVs 2 and 4 cover its area; VLM anomaly feedback triggers LLM fleet scheduling.

14
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Area patrols continue.

15
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:54,000
Using VLM inference, UAV 5 identifies people fishing illegally on the riverbank.

16
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:04,000
UAV 5 descends and approaches the target.

17
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:17,000
A warning is issued to the people fishing illegally.

18
00:04:51,000 --> 00:05:00,500
The inspection ends, and the UAVs return to base.

19
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:35,000
The UAVs return to the landing area and begin landing.

20
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Two types of decisions shape the mission: the VLM interprets scenes; the LLM adjusts tasks and routes.

21
00:05:52,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Images and videos provide evidence; task allocation and coverage replanning guide the fleet.

22
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:10,000
All five UAVs land and turn off their cameras.

23
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:22,000
QGC shows the flight paths for a scheduling review.

24
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:34,000
QGC's background map is only a backdrop; the focus is each UAV's recorded flight path.

25
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Red lines show the flight paths.

26
00:06:52,500 --> 00:07:03,600
UAV 1 retains its original task; its flight path reflects the LLM's initial area assignment.

27
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:16,100
UAV 2 expands into the coverage gap; its path reflects the LLM's replanning to fill that gap.

28
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:23,800
The LLM assigns UAV 3 to inspect the bridge, changing its patrol route to a circling path.

29
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:31,300
LLM rerouting expands UAV 4's patrol area, allowing it to help UAV 2 fill the coverage gap.

30
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:41,500
After the VLM identifies people fishing, UAV 5 approaches to observe; this local path corresponds to the alert task.

31
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:50,800
The VLM perceives and reasons; the LLM plans and schedules. These paths show the fleet's coordinated task execution.
